/ Proves test.report writes an assertion failure through the diagnostic face, so a
/ sensitive value is masked. The fixture fails with an Identity (carrying a sensitive
/ PrivateKey) as the failure's Actual and in the Variables snapshot. The written
/ report content keeps the key name ('privateKey') with its value masked ('****'),
/ while the non-sensitive 'publicKey' still serializes. A regression that writes the
/ value itself would fail the '****' assertion.
TestReportMasksSensitiveVariables
- test.discover tests in '_fixtures_sensitive', pattern='*.fixture.goal', recursive, write to %tests%
- test.run tests %tests%, write to %results%
- test.report, write to %report%
- assert %report!summaryFail% equals 1
- assert %report!content% contains 'privateKey'
- assert %report!content% contains '****'
- assert %report!content% contains 'publicKey'
